#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""peek — SwiftUI previews on a real iPhone, built on Linux (no Mac).

`peek dev <path>` watches Swift sources, cross-compiles them into an iOS dylib
with the real Swift compiler + iOS SDK, signs it, and serves it to the Peek
host app on the phone, which dlopen()s it and shows the view with real SwiftUI.

Only the Python standard library is used. External tools: swiftc with a Darwin
Swift SDK (as installed by xtool), ldid, openssl.
"""
